# Without types the two literals have a layout each, one with the field and one without. Object.hasOwn is then the question which layout the object has: one load of the word that says so, one comparison. No call, no lookup by name.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="step" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[options]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[shape]] = Load(b@[[options]], offset = 12, ControlDependent|ReadsImmutable|Reads:AOTObject_shapeWord, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[hasIt]] = Equal(b@[[shape]], {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK-NEXT: Branch(b@[[hasIt]], Terminal, {{*}}:TypeTest)
# CHECK: Double b@{{*}} = Load(b@[[options]], offset = 16, ControlDependent|Reads:ObjectFields{{*}}:GetSlot)
# CHECK-NOT: Branch(
# CHECK-NOT: Patchpoint(
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# X64: instructions: 6, patchpoints: 0
# ARM64: instructions: 7, patchpoints: 0
